  "summary": "The armistice over, Napoleon sent Oudinot with three corps to take Berlin. They marched by separate roads through the wooded country south of the city, out of touch with each other, and on the afternoon of the 23rd, in pouring rain, Reynier's Saxon corps took the village of Großbeeren on its own. At six Bülow's Prussian corps, attacking against Bernadotte's wishes, came on behind sixty guns and stormed the village with the bayonet and musket butt; Reynier's corps broke, and Oudinot fell back on Wittenberg.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "label": "Order of Battle for Gross-Beeren, 23 August 1813 (Nafziger Collection 813HGE)",
